= Evaluation Method  [EM-nn] =

//A candidate procedure for producing evidence. Surveyed in the Foundation; selected during Evaluation.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. EM-01, EM-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained — direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant — flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Measure or Evaluation Method, cite existing use in a validation study or authoritative literature (e.g. a validated-instrument source or textbook) instead.
|Procedure summary|what is actually done.
|Purpose|Verification (does the Function operate as specified?) or Validation (does it produce the intended effect?).
|Human subjects required|yes/no.
|Measures used|Measure ID(s).
|Cost and feasibility|what running it would require, realistically.
|Known limitations|what this method cannot establish, so it is not later asked to.

== Graph edges ==

produces → Evidence; applies → Measure.